cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the SVGX code, its format or its results, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "SVGX: Byte-Exact SVG Compression"
abstract: >-
  SVGX is a byte-exact compressor for SVG files. It predicts the control points
  of cubic Bézier curves from already decoded geometry with bounded exact integer
  arithmetic, restores the original decimal spelling of each coordinate with a
  value-conditioned model, and falls back to a whole-file Brotli stream with a
  zero-byte branch signal, so the output is never larger than that Brotli stream.
  The repository contains the encoder and decoder, an independent reference
  decoder, the frozen protocol, corpus manifests, all per-file measurements of
  the completed study and the scripts that regenerate its tables and figures,
  and a pre-specified follow-up (ablation of the prediction modes, comparison
  with paq8px, in-process timing) with its frozen protocol and results.
